# Runtime and data boundaries
- All customer/professional UI and public web APIs belong in `apps/web` deployed to Vercel. No extraction/reasoning agents or model provider credentials in Vercel/browser.
- All Readers, agents, Writer/analysis and canonical processing run on Oracle. `apps/reader` is Python/FastAPI for candidate extraction; `apps/worker` is TypeScript for workflow processing, verification, reconciliation and persistence.
- All application model calls go through the existing Oracle LiteLLM gateway with role-specific configured aliases; no direct provider call, bypass, or silent fallback. Alias ownership and gateway config are implementation-time (P2.1/P5.3); P0.2 error envelope and retry boundaries are approved in `docs/ERROR-HANDLING-RECOVERY.md`.
- Inngest orchestrates jobs/retries. Supabase stores private sources, access-controlled data, Canonical Study, snapshots and reports. Keep raw documents out of events/logs.
- One Hive has one evolving Canonical Study. Intents/results reuse that study; prior revisions remain inspectable. No source, no supported factual claim. Treat extraction proposals as untrusted until code verifies evidence anchors.
- `packages/core` remains domain-neutral. `domain-packs` are optional, declarative and version-pinned; pack-free intents must work. `packages/contracts` holds small versioned cross-service contracts; avoid runtime source imports across independently deployed apps.
- Prefer one production-equivalent processing path, minimal configuration and no speculative frameworks, parallel pipelines, activation registries or duplicate model-routing stacks.
- The repo documents designs, but does not itself imply Vercel/Oracle/Supabase are deployed or connected. Verify actual integrations before claiming success.
